<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Ultra Light on Typophile Archive</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/tags/ultra-light/</link><description>Recent content in Ultra Light on Typophile Archive</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 24 Jun 2013 08:28:00 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/tags/ultra-light/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Looking for light squarish slab serifs</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/104078/</link><pubDate>Mon, 24 Jun 2013 08:28:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/104078/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I am looking for a thin slab serif that has a bit of a contemporary or &amp;ldquo;tech&amp;rdquo; like feel without being cheesy. I have looked at &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20130820161539/http:/vllg.com/Constellation/Apex_Serif#panel=usage-poster"&gt;Apex Serif&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20130820161539/http:/www.myfonts.com/fonts/mellediete/gingar/"&gt;Gingar&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20130820161539/http:/www.myfonts.com/fonts/mti/soho/"&gt;Soho&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20130820161539/http:/www.typography.com/fonts/font_overview.php?productLineID=100036"&gt;Vitesse.&lt;/a&gt; These are all pretty close to what I want, but I am wondering what else is out there. Any ideas of other fonts in a similar vein?&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>